Fix: `Stack.evalStack` cannot build any stack.

`evalStack` wires `Layer.provideMerge(alchemy(dev), platform)`, providing
`platform` TO the layer that produces `AlchemyContext`. But `platform` contains
`Logger.layer([fileLogger("out")])`, and `fileLogger` opens with
`yield* AlchemyContext` to find the `.alchemy` directory to log into, while
`AlchemyContextLive` needs the `FileSystem` and `Path` that `platform` supplies.

The result is `Service not found: alchemy/Context` before a single resource is
examined — reproducible with a stack that has zero resources, `Layer.empty`
providers and no machine-run import at all.

This gives the logger layer its own context, built from the platform services it
actually needs, so nothing requiring `AlchemyContext` sits underneath the layer
that creates it.

Verified: with this applied, `Stack.evalStack` builds and planning proceeds to a
second, separate upstream defect (`Fiber.runLoop: Not a valid effect: undefined`)
which this patch does not address.

Delete this patch when upstream fixes the ordering. See docs/V2-PLAN.md.

--- a/node_modules/alchemy/src/Stack.ts
+++ b/node_modules/alchemy/src/Stack.ts
@@ -304,7 +304,15 @@
 const platform = Layer.mergeAll(
   PlatformServices,
   FetchHttpClient.layer,
-  Logger.layer([fileLogger("out")], { mergeWithExisting: true }),
+  // `fileLogger` reads `AlchemyContext` to find `.alchemy`, so the logger layer
+  // is given its own context built from the platform services it needs. Without
+  // this, `platform` requires a service that is only created above it, and every
+  // stack dies with `Service not found: alchemy/Context` before any resource is
+  // examined.
+  Layer.provide(
+    Logger.layer([fileLogger("out")], { mergeWithExisting: true }),
+    Layer.provide(AlchemyContextLive, PlatformServices),
+  ),
   Layer.provide(ProfileLive, PlatformServices),
   Layer.provide(CredentialsStoreLive, PlatformServices),
 );
